@host = https://localhost:7073
@fileId = 01a04ee4-b96a-7972-8c59-4100be5dc598
@token = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 0. Upload a file first — reuse requests/download.http #0, then paste
###    the returned id into @fileId above.

### 1. Create a download ticket (should 201 Created)
###    Copy the returned token into @token above.
POST {{host}}/api/DownloadTickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fileId": "{{fileId}}"
}

### 2. Create a ticket for a file that doesn't exist (should 404)
POST {{host}}/api/DownloadTickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fileId": "99999999-9999-9999-9999-999999999999"
}

### 3. Create a ticket with an empty body (should 400)
POST {{host}}/api/DownloadTickets
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 4. Download with a valid ticket (should 200, file content)
###    Add ?resolution=thumbnail etc. to pull a variant instead.
GET {{host}}/api/DownloadTickets/{{token}}

### 5. Download with a token that isn't a guid (should 400 from route constraint)
GET {{host}}/api/DownloadTickets/not-a-guid

### 6. Download with a well-formed but unknown token (should 404)
GET {{host}}/api/DownloadTickets/99999999-9999-9999-9999-999999999999

### 7. Download with an expired ticket (should 404)
###    Set "DownloadTickets": { "ValidForMinutes": 1 } in appsettings, create a
###    ticket via #1, wait a minute+, then hit its token again.
GET {{host}}/api/DownloadTickets/{{token}}
